# .agent/projects.local — per-machine project registry (issue #227, #172 step 2;
# parent roots and trailing fields: issue #265)
#
# Copy this file to .agent/projects.local (gitignored). The registry is the
# only link between the workspace and the projects it serves; a project may
# live anywhere on disk.
#
# One project per line, whitespace-separated:
#
#   <name>  <project_type>  [<path>]  [key=value ...]
#
#   name          Project identity on this machine. Also the worktree repo
#                 key and (for now) the default hosting dir projects/<name>.
#                 Allowed: [A-Za-z0-9._-], must start with a letter or
#                 digit; '..' is not allowed.
#   project_type  Adapter type; must exist at .agent/project_types/<type>/
#                 (ADR-0011). Currently: single_project, ros2_colcon.
#                 The pseudo-type "project" declares a PARENT ROOT: a
#                 directory that groups several instances of one project
#                 (e.g. one per ROS distro). It has no adapter and need not
#                 be a git repository; it is the session and memory unit.
#   path          Optional hosting directory (absolute, or relative to the
#                 workspace root; default projects/<name>). No spaces.
#   key=value     Optional trailing fields (no spaces in values):
#                   parent=<name>            this line is an instance of
#                                            parent root <name>
#                   worktrees=<path>         where this root's worktrees
#                                            live (default <path>/worktrees)
#                   role=<name>              passed to the adapter as
#                                            ACTIVE_PROJECT_ROLE
#                   distro=<name>            passed to the adapter as
#                                            ACTIVE_PROJECT_DISTRO; for
#                                            ros2_colcon this is the ROS
#                                            distro (overrides ROS_DISTRO in
#                                            projects.d/<name>.sh; must agree
#                                            with the manifest if that names
#                                            one)
#                   default_instance=<name>  parent lines only: the instance
#                                            used when the parent is
#                                            selected without --project
#
# single_project checkouts are managed manually: clone the project into
# its hosting dir, then register it here. ros2_colcon instances bootstrap
# themselves from an empty hosting dir — register the name, point
# MANIFEST_BOOTSTRAP_URL at the project's bootstrap.yaml, and run
# `.agent/scripts/adapter --project <name> setup` (or `make build
# PROJECT=<name>` after setup). Per-project build/test commands go in
# .agent/projects.d/<name>.sh (gitignored), with .agent/project_config.sh
# as the shared fallback. A ros2_colcon config looks like:
#
#   # .agent/projects.d/p11-jazzy.sh
#   MANIFEST_BOOTSTRAP_URL="https://<host>/<manifest-repo>/raw/jazzy/config/bootstrap.yaml"
#
# One instance per distro: a second distro of the same project is a second
# registry entry with its OWN hosting dir. Group them under a parent root
# so sessions, memory and instructions have one home. Never point two
# entries at one dir — setup reuses an existing manifest checkout with only
# a warning on a branch mismatch, so the second instance would silently
# read the first one's manifest.
#
# How the active project is resolved (adapter dispatcher):
#   1. --project <name> (or: make build PROJECT=<name>)
#   2. current directory inside a registered hosting dir (longest match, so
#      a cwd inside an instance resolves to the instance, not its parent)
#   3. legacy project/ symlink (unchanged behavior)
#   A parent root selected by 1 or 2 resolves to its default_instance, else
#   its only instance; several instances without a default is an error
#   that lists them.
#
# Examples:
#gz4d         single_project  /home/me/src/gz4d
#coastal      single_project  /data/checkouts/coastal_mapper
#p11          project         /home/me/project11-ng          default_instance=p11-rolling
#p11-jazzy    ros2_colcon     /home/me/project11-ng/jazzy    parent=p11 distro=jazzy   role=dev
#p11-rolling  ros2_colcon     /home/me/project11-ng/rolling  parent=p11 distro=rolling role=dev
